Haiku is not a KMS platform, so Mesa skips dep_libdrm. RADV still calls
drmGetVersion and the drm syncobj helpers. Look the dependency up when
the amd driver is enabled. This does not add Haiku to the KMS list.

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -1693,10 +1693,10 @@ endif
 allow_fallback_for_libdrm = get_option('allow-fallback-for').contains('libdrm')
 
 with_gallium_drisw_kms = false
-if system_has_kms_drm
+if system_has_kms_drm or with_amd_vk
   dep_libdrm = dependency(
     'libdrm', version : '>=' + _drm_ver,
-    required : with_dri2 or with_dri or with_gbm,
+    required : with_dri2 or with_dri or with_gbm or with_amd_vk,
     allow_fallback: allow_fallback_for_libdrm,
   )
 else
